    "plan": "{\n  \"architecture\": {\n    \"components\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-world\",\n        \"name\": \"Authoritative physical world\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own committed and trial state, SI-derived two-dimensional units, configuration, requested and actual time, advancement and bounded failure results. Physical state and advancement are independent of Bitloop Scene, rendering and serialization.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"name\": \"Membrane and supports\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own membrane positions, velocities, membrane mass, elastic parameters and support constraints. Compute geometry-dependent passive and contractile forces, stored energy and support reactions. Detect unsupported geometry rather than repairing it.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"name\": \"Reduced contained material\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own fixed carrier mass and reference thermodynamic parameters. Derive pressure, stored compression energy and reduced inertia from actual chamber geometry and wall motion. Internal fuel and nutrient inventories belong to C-resources, not duplicate compartment state.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-fluid\",\n        \"name\": \"Shared exterior fluid\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own one environmental grid, exterior carrier momentum and pressure-solve state. Advance incompressible flow and viscosity on the exterior regions supplied by C-boundary; account for outer-reservoir fluxes and work.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-boundary\",\n        \"name\": \"Geometry and paired exchanges\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Derive occupied regions, apertures and swept volumes from authoritative membrane geometry. Supply compatible wall fluxes, pressure traction, impermeability and paired mechanical/species exchange records. These are trial-step derived quantities, not independent material inventories.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-resources\",\n        \"name\": \"Nutrient, fuel and activity\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own environmental nutrient amounts, internal nutrient and fuel inventories, reaction/source accounts and deterministic actuator requests. Use C-fluid transport and C-boundary permeability; authorize affordable mechanical work without directly prescribing motion.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-experiment\",\n        \"name\": \"Construction, observation and evidence\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Build fixtures, request simulated intervals and read committed observation views. Keep Substrate/Substrate.h and .cpp thin; reuse Bitloop headless telemetry, drawing and snapshots. Retain reproducible commands, configurations, semantic evidence and inspected images without embedding diagnostic formats in physical laws.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"decisions\": [\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use a project-owned physical core with a thin Bitloop adapter. Reuse existing build, lifecycle, headless trace and snapshot facilities; introduce no editor, checkpoint system, generic transaction framework or simulation-side task orchestration.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-core\",\n        \"rationale\": \"One authoritative simulation must support both visible and headless experiments while remaining independently buildable. Framework changes and new dependencies require explicit authorization.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use area as represented volume, constant exterior areal density and explicitly declared two-dimensional force, pressure, viscosity and energy units. Every inventory has one owner; pressure is a constraint variable, and geometry and concentrations are derived.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-units\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This avoids hidden thickness conversions, duplicate inventories and confusion between resource amounts and concentrations. D1 and D2 establish the concrete unit and ownership tables.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"The provisional candidate is a fixed-topology polygonal elastic membrane, geometry-dependent barotropic contents with reduced interior inertia, and a shared Cartesian staggered incompressible exterior using conservative moving cut-cell geometry. Supports prevent contact; an open pressure reservoir accommodates changes of excluded area.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-candidate\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This matches explicit structures, spatial external flow and inexpensive unresolved contents. Springs, pressure energy, interior interpolation and cut-cell stabilization are hypotheses to derive in D3-D7, not accepted methods. The open reservoir avoids the incompatibility of changing chamber area inside a sealed incompressible domain. No silent solver substitution is permitted.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Initially restrict fixtures to separated, simple, star-shaped chambers with declared minimum edge, feature, separation and grid-resolution limits. Propose a centroid-fan linear interior velocity reduction with a geometry-dependent mass matrix; derive its kinetic energy and shape terms before implementation.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-reduction\",\n        \"rationale\": \"A bounded geometry family makes a concrete contents-inertia candidate possible without pretending to resolve interior circulation. D4 must show rigid-motion and deformation consistency and identify excluded motions; failure requires an explicit design amendment.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use a tightly coupled implicit candidate step with a compatible pressure/structure exchange. A step starts from immutable committed state, predicts geometry and affordable activity, repeatedly rebuilds trial geometry and solves fluid/structure exchange, then performs conservative species/reaction updates and checks all balances before atomic commit. Every rejected attempt restores all trial physical, inventory, actuator and diagnostic-account state and retries the same interval within frozen limits.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-step\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Moving excluded volume, added mass, work pairing and fuel affordability cannot be independent afterthoughts. D7 and D8 must replace this sequence outline with discrete equations, exact time levels, iteration variables, affordability feedback, stopping rules and rollback contents before implementation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Use dilute environmental nutrient with negligible carrier-mass effects, finite-rate membrane transfer, explicit conversion to fuel and a declared negative-actuator-work policy. Nutrient permeability never permits bulk-fluid leakage.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-resources\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This provides conservative resource limitation without introducing mixtures or thermal physics. D8 defines positivity, energy units, reaction stoichiometry and near-empty behavior.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Freeze physical cases, local and cumulative error/damping limits, horizons, retry limits and experiment budgets before candidate evaluation. Human approval gates implementation; passive qualification gates resources; active single-chamber qualification gates the 16-chamber screen.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-gates\",\n        \"rationale\": \"A failed or inconclusive foundation test must stop expansion, not trigger automatic tolerance relaxation, unbounded optimization or undocumented changes in physical behavior.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Keep future tissue, contact, internal flow, openings, growth and controllers outside this implementation. Preserve physical boundaries through explicit force/reaction, geometry/flux, inventory-transfer and action-request contracts, not plugin systems.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-scope\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The prototype can inform the eventual engine without implementing speculative extensibility. Passing a supported, separated-body screen does not establish locomotion or freely interacting organisms.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"decision\": \"Record design contracts in project architecture documentation and task execution state only in MindGraph. Each decision-bearing report must include substantive observations in summary, checks[].name, issues and plan_concern, with artifact paths as supporting evidence.\",\n        \"id\": \"AD-evidence\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Reviewers cannot inspect local paths. Reports must distinguish measured evidence from declarations, document commands/build/configuration identity, and expose negative or inconclusive findings.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-world\",\n        \"relationship\": \"owns state containers and coordinates trial advancement, validation and atomic commit across\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-world\",\n        \"relationship\": \"coordinates reduced pressure and inertia contributions from\",\n        \"to\": \"C-contents\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-world\",\n        \"relationship\": \"coordinates shared exterior advancement by\",\n        \"to\": \"C-fluid\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-world\",\n        \"relationship\": \"coordinates conservative inventory and activity updates by\",\n        \"to\": \"C-resources\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"relationship\": \"provides oriented geometry and wall motion to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-boundary\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"relationship\": \"returns geometry-dependent pressure forces and inertia to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-boundary\",\n        \"relationship\": \"supplies fluid regions, swept volumes and impermeability constraints to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-fluid\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-fluid\",\n        \"relationship\": \"returns compatible pressure/viscous tractions and reservoir accounts through\",\n        \"to\": \"C-boundary\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-boundary\",\n        \"relationship\": \"returns paired fluid loads and exchange work to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-fluid\",\n        \"relationship\": \"supplies conservative transport fluxes to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-resources\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-resources\",\n        \"relationship\": \"supplies affordable actuator requests to\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-resources\",\n        \"relationship\": \"uses membrane measure and conservative permeability exchanges from\",\n        \"to\": \"C-boundary\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-experiment\",\n        \"relationship\": \"constructs fixtures, requests advancement and reads committed observations from\",\n        \"to\": \"C-world\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"summary\": \"Build one supported chamber using a deliberately bounded, provisional numerical candidate: a polygonal membrane, barotropic reduced contents with explicit inertia, and an open-reservoir incompressible exterior on a shared moving cut-cell grid. First derive and reconcile its numerical contracts, then obtain human approval, implement a passive coupled path, and test feasibility before adding resources or presentation. Authoritative records comprise membrane kinematics/mass, contents parameters, exterior momentum, species amounts, fuel, time and explicit exchange accounts; observation views expose committed values only. D2-D8 define their exact shapes and D9 freezes the common interfaces and complete advancement sequence. Later engine responsibilities fit these ownership and exchange boundaries but receive no implementation tasks in this plan.\"\n  },\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-regime\",\n      \"statement\": \"A low-Mach incompressible exterior with a declared pressure reservoir is an acceptable first physical experiment. D1 must justify the regime, outer placement and inflow/outflow behavior; this is not a user-approved numerical choice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-geometry\",\n      \"statement\": \"Restricting the first fixtures to star-shaped, separated chambers can still demonstrate meaningful deformation, transport and shared-fluid interaction. Feature limits and detection behavior must be approved at D9.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-inertia\",\n      \"statement\": \"A centroid-fan velocity reduction may provide adequate inertia for the supported chamber without resolving internal flow. D4 derivations and I9 evidence must establish its applicability, including non-rigid deformation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-workflow\",\n      \"statement\": \"The supplied Bitloop facilities may be usable in the active target, but telemetry hooks, commands, runner behavior and independent-build support are unverified. I1 must establish the actual seam and report unavailable checks honestly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AS-cost\",\n      \"statement\": \"Access to a Ryzen 9 9950X3D and controlled measurement conditions is not established. The required pilot target remains one simulated second per wall-clock second with at most 16 CPU workers; unavailable target hardware makes that conclusion inconclusive, not transferable from another machine.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"D1-D9 supply one reconciled candidate, frozen proposed acceptance limits and implementation-consumer mappings.\",\n        \"The workflow checkpoint and explicit design approval are recorded before substantive implementation.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Grouping record only. Children produce the design and approvals; this milestone does not duplicate their work. Implementation remains conditional on those outputs.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Establish an understandable, implementable and explicitly approved numerical experiment.\",\n      \"id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design and approve the foundation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The existing target compiles in a Codex-owned build context without changing user build state.\",\n        \"A real headless run emits deterministic initial and advanced time/state values through the actual telemetry hook; the report quotes the values and repeat-run comparison.\",\n        \"Retain exact commands, target/build/configuration identity, scene selection and evidence under .codex/runs/runNNNN_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS/; report independent-build availability and limitations.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"I1 uses capabilities bitloop (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md) and traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; references/tracing-diagnostics.md beneath that skill). Workers inspect applicable repository guidance, active headers and build target. Implement only a minimal deterministic observable and adapter seam, not a solver. Framework/other-owner changes or new dependencies require explicit authorization.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Establish actual execution and evidence capture before relying on framework declarations.\",\n      \"id\": \"I1\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Establish the real execution/evidence seam\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Present I1's commands, observed values and saved result to the human for manual inspection.\",\n        \"Record human confirmation of execution, review and save/reload; otherwise leave this checkpoint incomplete.\",\n        \"Document how dependency-ready leaves and review outcomes will be confirmed manually if the host does not enforce them.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I1's captured report, not merely artifact paths. This is a human workflow checkpoint, not simulation code or a review-engine implementation. Design derivations may proceed, but D9 and substantial implementation depend on this confirmation.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I1\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Verify the real planning/execution/evidence workflow once.\",\n      \"id\": \"H-workflow\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Confirm the execution and saved-review workflow\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Publish units, regime, geometry, coefficients, supports, meaningful activity/transport amplitudes and reservoir conditions with justification.\",\n        \"Define independently calculable reference cases and local/global volume, momentum, resource and energy metrics, including local and cumulative numerical-damping limits.\",\n        \"Propose numerical thresholds, refinement comparisons, timescale-derived smoke/behavioral/endurance horizons and finite retry/experiment budgets before evaluation.\",\n        \"Separate requirements from provisional choices; define the 16-body workload specification and what must be frozen before timing.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-resources\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"D1 consumes the vision and AD-units, AD-candidate, AD-gates, AS-regime. Produce the Experiment and Budgets section of project architecture documentation. Use capability simulation-health (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md) to design proportionate horizons and monitors, not claim existing oracles. No production solver work.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Turn the physical demonstration into a bounded, measurable experiment.\",\n      \"id\": \"D1\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define the physical experiment and budgets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Specify concrete committed/trial records, fixed-topology identities, configuration, requested/actual time, failure result and read-only observation view.\",\n        \"Assign one owner to each carrier mass, momentum, nutrient amount, fuel, stored energy and cumulative source/reaction account; identify derived quantities and pressure-solve caches.\",\n        \"Give a worked step accounting example including membrane/content inertia, reservoir exchange and resource transfer without duplicate inventory.\",\n        \"Define state equality/fingerprint coverage for rollback checks.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-resources\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1's unit/regime/fixture specification. Under AD-core and AD-units, produce the State and Ownership contract consumed by D3-D8 and I2. Distinguish ownership of amounts from where equations are evaluated; exclude serialization frameworks and future variable-topology identity machinery.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Define the minimal shared state and ownership contract.\",\n      \"id\": \"D2\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define authoritative state and ownership\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Derive membrane energy, force gradients, mass assignment and any necessary bending term; justify included terms against D1's behavior.\",\n        \"Specify orientation, area/area derivatives, supported deformations, support constraints, reaction and support-work accounting.\",\n        \"Provide a small force/energy calculation and supported equilibrium/deformation expectations with tolerances.\",\n        \"Define mechanics input/output records and unsupported-geometry failure checks.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1 fixture/budgets and D2 kinematic/state records. AD-candidate proposes an elastic polygon, not an approved spring formula. Produce the Mechanics contract: geometry, constitutive derivatives, forces and constraint interface consumed by D4, D6, D7 and I3. No contact, self-intersection repair or general tissue library.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\",\n        \"D2\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Derive an implementable membrane/support model.\",\n      \"id\": \"D3\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design membrane and support mechanics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Specify pressure versus actual area and stored energy satisfying the declared pressure-work derivative and stable supported operating range.\",\n        \"Derive the candidate reduced velocity field, mass matrix, kinetic energy and geometry-dependent inertial terms; do not double-count contents mass at membrane vertices.\",\n        \"Derive compression, deformation, rigid translation and rotation checks, including reactions and work.\",\n        \"Explain excluded internal flows, validity scales and the smallest resolving experiment for any unresolved reduction risk.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1-D3, particularly oriented geometry, wall degrees of freedom and force/constraint interface. Under AD-reduction and AS-inertia, examine the centroid-fan candidate and retain one justified formulation or report a necessary amendment. Produce the Contents contract for D5/D7/I4; no spatial internal-flow solver.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\",\n        \"D2\",\n        \"D3\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Give enclosed material physically accounted pressure and inertia.\",\n      \"id\": \"D4\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design pressure-bearing contents\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Specify grid storage, control volumes, momentum transport, viscosity, pressure operator, wall terms and units.\",\n        \"Define reservoir pressure, backflow/inflow data, outer flux/work accounting and compatibility of changing excluded area with D4.\",\n        \"Specify solver residual scaling, convergence/failure criteria and discrete dissipation accounting.\",\n        \"Derive a stationary-boundary equilibrium and independently calculable flow reference with boundary and resolution assumptions.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-fluid\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1 units/regime/budgets, D2 fluid records and D4 area/pressure behavior. AD-candidate provisionally selects a staggered incompressible exterior with an open reservoir. Produce the Exterior Fluid contract for D6/D7/I5. Establish a minimum stationary-boundary scheme before moving geometry; no turbulence or adaptive grid.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\",\n        \"D2\",\n        \"D4\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Define a conservative exterior fluid step with a physical volume accommodation.\",\n      \"id\": \"D5\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design the exterior fluid step\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Specify polygon-to-fluid-region construction, face apertures, oriented boundary measures and swept-volume calculations.\",\n        \"Give a worked moving-wall example demonstrating per-cell volume change, swept flux and outer-volume compatibility.\",\n        \"Choose one concrete tiny-region and cell-crossing treatment with conservative state redistribution; define supported region connectivity and how unsupported split/narrow regions are detected.\",\n        \"State feature limits, degeneracy tolerances and impermeability guarantees without silently erasing geometry or introducing unaccounted material.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D3 geometry/motion, D4 area response and D5 control-volume/flux definitions. Produce the Geometry and Flux contract for D7/D8/I6/I7. Cut cells are a candidate requiring an actual geometric conservation law and bounded handling of small regions, not permission to invent arbitrary volume corrections.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D3\",\n        \"D4\",\n        \"D5\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Make moving occupied geometry and transported volume locally compatible.\",\n      \"id\": \"D6\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design moving geometry and conservative fluxes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Write the actual discrete structure/contents/fluid equations, pressure-to-wall and wall-to-fluid operators, reaction pairs and work identities.\",\n        \"Specify time levels, predictors, repeated coupling variables, geometry rebuilds, convergence norms, timestep restrictions and bounded retries.\",\n        \"Trace one full accepted step and one rejected attempt, listing restored records and preserved actual time.\",\n        \"Identify added-mass, tiny-cell and solver conditioning risks plus complete-step cost drivers; define corresponding I9 observations.\",\n        \"State physical dissipation, numerical residual and local/cumulative damping accounts separately.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D2-D6 state, energies, inertia, pressure equations and swept-volume contracts. Replace AD-step's outline with the Accepted Advancement contract used by I2/I7/I8. Select and explain one concrete implicit exchange solve/iteration; 'use a coupled solve' is not a deliverable. If a bounded disposable probe is necessary, follow simulation-health (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md) and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/temporary-diagnostics.md, keep it development-only and report negative findings.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D2\",\n        \"D3\",\n        \"D4\",\n        \"D5\",\n        \"D6\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Resolve discrete two-way exchange and atomic accepted advancement.\",\n      \"id\": \"D7\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design two-way coupling and accepted advancement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Define positive conservative scalar transport on D6 regions and D7 time levels, including diffusion/advection and reservoir source accounting as appropriate to D1.\",\n        \"Specify finite-rate paired uptake, donor limits, conversion stoichiometry, chemical/fuel energy units and explicit reactions.\",\n        \"Define local actuator force requests, positive-work affordability and negative-work policy; resolve near-zero fuel without prescribed animation or numerical-energy harvesting.\",\n        \"Trace depleted/replenished and rejected steps, including any mechanics/resource iteration required to prevent overspending.\",\n        \"State the dilute-carrier approximation and its validity; update the shared ownership/exchange definitions where necessary.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1 resource cases, D2 inventory ownership, D6 geometry/flux and D7 trial exchange/work. Under AD-resources, produce the Resource and Activity contract consumed by I10-I12. No biological controller, growth or heat system; negative work must be explicitly accounted rather than automatically becoming fuel.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\",\n        \"D2\",\n        \"D6\",\n        \"D7\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Make transport and affordable actuation part of the same conservative step.\",\n      \"id\": \"D8\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Design nutrient transfer and fuel-limited work\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Publish one reconciled contract with concrete state/exchange interfaces and a complete read-predict-solve-exchange-check-commit sequence, including time levels, iterations and rejection.\",\n        \"Resolve cross-document units, ownership, volume compatibility, support/reservoir work and resource affordability inconsistencies.\",\n        \"Present candidate equations, reference calculations, proposed frozen thresholds, budgets, assumptions and unresolved issues substantively in the report, not only as links.\",\n        \"Map every I2-I15 task to exact design sections, inputs, outputs and focused checks; submit explicit MindGraph proposals to amend or split tasks made inaccurate or vague by the design.\",\n        \"Record I1 workflow limitations and prepare a concise human approval package; unresolved blocking choices prevent implementation release.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D1-D8, I1's actual seam and H-workflow confirmation. Apply AD-evidence: architecture documentation explains contracts, while MindGraph owns readiness and changes. This reconciles rather than implements the solver. Implementation leaves are provisional until affected task amendments and explicit human approval are complete.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D1\",\n        \"D2\",\n        \"D3\",\n        \"D4\",\n        \"D5\",\n        \"D6\",\n        \"D7\",\n        \"D8\",\n        \"H-workflow\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Make one candidate and its downstream implementation genuinely ready for approval.\",\n      \"id\": \"D9\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do D1-D8 and the demonstrated workflow make AD-candidate, AD-reduction and AD-step implementable within the frozen experiment budgets, or do unresolved inertia, moving-volume, coupling or affordability issues require specific architecture/task amendments before human approval?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Reconcile the design and make implementation ready\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Obtain explicit human approval of the numerical candidate, supported geometry, frozen acceptance limits, horizons and experiment budgets.\",\n        \"Confirm D9 review findings and required task amendments are resolved before releasing I2.\",\n        \"Record that approval permits the experiment and does not certify the physics; rejection or requested changes leave implementation blocked.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes D9's substantive approval package and review outcome. This is an explicit human decision, not an automatic approval inferred from a completed design task. No code changes.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"D9\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Authorize the bounded foundation experiment.\",\n      \"id\": \"H-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-design\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Approve the candidate and frozen experiment limits\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"I2-I8 deliver the minimum physically coupled passive path and focused component checks.\",\n        \"I9 supplies reproducible continue/reject/inconclusive evidence before resource or substantial presentation expansion.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Grouping record only. Children implement the approved contracts; no general-purpose numerical libraries or optimization campaign.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Establish whether the passive coupled primitive is a viable foundation.\",\n      \"id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement and evaluate the passive coupled primitive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement approved committed/trial records, requested versus actual time and bounded result/error reporting without Scene dependencies.\",\n        \"An intentionally rejected update preserves all authoritative state and time; partial accepted advancement reports its actual endpoint and never skips the failed interval.\",\n        \"Non-finite or invalid state cannot commit; deterministic repeated advancement uses I1's verified observable.\",\n        \"Document implemented observation and advancement interfaces for downstream workers.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I1 seam and D2/D7 contracts reconciled by D9. Not execution-ready until H-design and any D9 task amendments are complete. Implement a local trial-state mechanism under AD-core/AD-step, not a generic transaction system. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md) for actual failure/time evidence.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I1\",\n        \"H-design\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Provide atomic physical advancement and read-only committed observation.\",\n      \"id\": \"I2\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement core state and atomic advancement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement D3 geometry, passive forces, mass and support constraints through I2's state interface.\",\n        \"Focused energy-gradient and reaction checks meet frozen limits; D3 equilibrium and supported-deformation cases match predictions.\",\n        \"Unsupported orientation, self-intersection and declared feature violations return explicit invalid-geometry results without repair.\",\n        \"Expose the agreed geometry/motion/force interface for contents and moving-boundary consumers.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-world\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes approved D3 Mechanics contract and I2 records/failure semantics. Scope is fixed-topology passive mechanics and support reactions; no actuation, contact or rendering. Include implementation and the small reference checks together.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I2\",\n        \"D3\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver force-driven membrane/support mechanics.\",\n      \"id\": \"I3\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement membrane and support mechanics\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Contents pressure and compression energy use actual membrane area and meet the approved pressure-work checks.\",\n        \"Implement D4 reduced inertia including required geometry-dependent terms; total carrier mass is not duplicated.\",\n        \"Compression/deformation and rigid translation/rotation checks meet approved predictions for kinetic energy, forces and support accounts.\",\n        \"Invalid area or reduction geometry fails through I2 without committing.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-structure\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes approved D4 Contents contract and I3 wall kinematics/constraints. Conditional on the D9-approved reduction, not on a worker choosing a new inertia model. Produce a combined passive chamber mechanics contribution for I8; no exterior coupling yet.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I3\",\n        \"D4\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Attach physically accounted contents pressure and inertia to the membrane.\",\n      \"id\": \"I4\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement compartment pressure and inertia\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement D5 grid state, transport/viscosity, pressure operator, outer conditions and solver failure criteria for stationary boundaries.\",\n        \"Equilibrium and independently calculable flow cases meet frozen local-field, balance and convergence limits.\",\n        \"Reservoir flux/work and physical versus numerical dissipation are observable; failed solves do not commit.\",\n        \"Provide the grid/flux/pressure interfaces consumed by I6 and I7.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I2 state/time and approved D5 Exterior Fluid contract. Scope is the minimum stationary-boundary exterior, not moving geometry. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md) for bounded temporal evidence; implement the required semantic metrics rather than assuming generated hooks contain them.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I2\",\n        \"D5\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Verify the exterior fluid discretization before boundary motion.\",\n      \"id\": \"I5\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement a stationary-boundary fluid reference\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Produce fluid regions, apertures, oriented boundary measures and swept volumes using D6's algorithms.\",\n        \"Cell-crossing tests satisfy per-cell and global volume identities, including creation/disappearance of permitted regions.\",\n        \"Tiny-region, narrow-feature and connectivity cases either satisfy approved treatment or explicitly reject; no silent geometry erasure or inventory loss.\",\n        \"Geometry failure leaves I2 committed state intact and reports the offending feature.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-fluid\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I3 geometry, I5 grid storage and approved D6 Geometry and Flux contract. This work produces geometric operators and tests only; dynamic wall-fluid response belongs to I7. Do not independently redesign stabilization or feature limits.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I3\",\n        \"I5\",\n        \"D6\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Implement locally conservative moving fluid geometry.\",\n      \"id\": \"I6\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement moving-boundary geometry\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Advance the exterior under the approved controlled wall-motion fixture using I6 swept fluxes and D7 time levels.\",\n        \"Measure local impermeability, transported volumes, reservoir accommodation and reaction/work accounts against frozen reference limits.\",\n        \"Exercise cell-crossing and timestep refinement without unaccounted fluid sources.\",\n        \"Keep prescribed motion confined to a test fixture; expose response operators for I8.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I5 fluid step, I6 geometry and D7 pressure/wall exchange contract. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md) for actual flux/work values. This does not satisfy the force-driven organism deliverable.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I5\",\n        \"I6\",\n        \"D7\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Verify conservative moving-wall fluid response independently of free coupling.\",\n      \"id\": \"I7\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement conservative fluid response to prescribed wall motion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement D7's equations/iteration with I4 chamber mechanics and I7 response; active wall motion follows forces and constraints.\",\n        \"Passive equilibrium and pressure perturbation cases satisfy paired-force, support/reservoir-work and energy residual checks.\",\n        \"An intentionally nonconvergent exchange restores geometry, fluid, chamber state, accounts and time; retry/failure respects frozen limits.\",\n        \"Expose committed coupled observations and convergence/retry metrics for I9 and later presentation.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I4, I7 and the approved D7 Accepted Advancement contract. Reuse component checks rather than hardening them into general libraries. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md). Produce the earliest actual passive coupled path; resource features remain excluded.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I4\",\n        \"I7\",\n        \"D7\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Close the two-way mechanical exchange with atomic acceptance.\",\n      \"id\": \"I8\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement two-way chamber-fluid exchange\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Run frozen passive references and timestep/spatial refinement with documented configuration and unchanged limits.\",\n        \"Cover the D1/D7 repeated-motion and relaxation horizons using continuous hard-condition monitors plus selected complete-state inspections.\",\n        \"Report local leakage, region degeneracy, field/feature errors, work residuals, damping, convergence, retries and preliminary complete-step cost numerically.\",\n        \"Extend unresolved drift only within the agreed budget; report continue/reject/inconclusive and remaining uncertainty even when the experiment itself ran successfully.\",\n        \"Provide a reproducible human-runnable command and self-contained findings, with retained evidence under .codex/runs/.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I8 and frozen D1/D9 cases. Capabilities: simulation-health (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md and temporary-diagnostics.md) and traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; references/tracing-diagnostics.md). Record dt, ticks, physical timescales, inspection schedule, worst observations and stopping rationale. No tolerance relaxation, resource implementation or prolonged optimization; negative evidence reaches review under AD-evidence.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I8\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether the passive numerical candidate supports further investment.\",\n      \"id\": \"I9\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-passive\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do the frozen passive cases, refinement and repeated-motion evidence support AD-candidate/AD-reduction/AD-step, especially local impermeability, reduced inertia, work pairing and bounded coupling cost, or must resource work stop for a specific redesign or inconclusive finding?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Evaluate the passive coupled candidate\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"I10-I12 deliver conservative transport, finite-rate uptake/conversion and genuinely fuel-limited force-driven activity.\",\n        \"I13 presents the same committed simulation visibly, and I14 supplies a single-chamber foundation decision using frozen thresholds.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Grouping record only. Resource children are conditional on I9's accepted foundation; substantial visual work does not precede that evidence.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Demonstrate a resource-limited active chamber and qualify its physical behavior.\",\n      \"id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add resources and qualify the active single chamber\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement D8 scalar amounts and conservative positive transport using the existing moving regions and fluid fluxes.\",\n        \"Approved gradient/reference cases meet positivity, local-feature and total balance limits including reservoir sources/sinks.\",\n        \"Zero-permeability moving-wall cases show no nutrient crossing the membrane and no unaccounted amount during cell transitions.\",\n        \"Rejected advancement preserves scalar inventories and source accounts.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes accepted I9 foundation, D8 transport contract and I6/I8 geometry/advancement through that dependency chain. Do not start on reject/inconclusive evidence unless an explicit reviewed amendment releases it. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md). Scope excludes uptake and actuation.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I9\",\n        \"D8\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Transport environmental nutrient conservatively on the actual moving exterior.\",\n      \"id\": \"I10\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement environmental nutrient transport\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Implement D8 finite-rate uptake with equal-and-opposite environmental/internal transfers and explicit conversion reactions.\",\n        \"Zero permeability, finite-rate reference, near-empty donor and exhausted-donor cases meet positivity and balance limits.\",\n        \"Carrier impermeability remains unchanged by nutrient permeability.\",\n        \"Injected rejection leaves all internal/environmental inventories and conversion/source accounts unchanged.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-world\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I10 scalar state and approved D8 membrane-transfer, conversion and rollback contracts. Produce internal nutrient/fuel inventory updates for I12. No controller or growth; the dilute-carrier approximation remains explicit.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I10\",\n        \"D8\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Supply fuel through physically accounted membrane transport and conversion.\",\n      \"id\": \"I11\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement membrane uptake and conversion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Apply deterministic local force requests through the approved D8 affordability algorithm, not prescribed deformation.\",\n        \"Mechanical positive work cannot exceed the authorized fuel budget within frozen tolerances; negative work follows the approved policy.\",\n        \"Demonstrate depletion reducing activity and replenishment restoring it with explicit source/reaction/work accounting.\",\n        \"Near-zero fuel, affordability-iteration failure and rejected steps cannot overspend, double-debit or partially commit.\",\n        \"Produce an active single-chamber fixture and committed activity/fuel metrics for I13/I14.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-world\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I11 inventories, accepted I8/I9 coupling and approved D8 force-request/work/rollback contract. Use traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md) for depletion/replenishment and work evidence. Scope is deterministic experimental activity, not an artificial-life controller.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I11\",\n        \"D8\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Make contraction physically force-driven and resource-limited.\",\n      \"id\": \"I12\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement work-limited actuation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A runnable Bitloop example displays committed membrane deformation, exterior flow and internal fuel with clear scales/labels.\",\n        \"Drawing does not mutate physics; equivalent requested simulated intervals give matching authoritative observations headlessly and visibly within declared tolerances.\",\n        \"Inspect snapshots from meaningful deformation, depletion and replenishment states and correlate them with semantic metrics.\",\n        \"Record exact launch/capture configuration and observed image content; keep Substrate adapter files thin.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-experiment\",\n        \"C-world\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I12 active fixture and I8/I2 committed observation interface. Capabilities: bitloop (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md) and snapshots-checkpoints (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/checkpoints-snapshots.md and visual-qa.md). Use snapshots only, not unimplemented checkpoint hooks. No editor, scripted interaction requirement or visual polish campaign.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I12\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Make the authoritative coupled experiment understandable on screen.\",\n      \"id\": \"I13\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Make the coupled experiment visible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Run combined active cases and timestep/spatial refinement against unchanged approved thresholds.\",\n        \"Cover transport, repeated deformation, depletion and replenishment timescales and extend beyond the first healthy window within the agreed endurance budget.\",\n        \"Report local fields/features, impermeability, inventories, reaction/source balances, fuel/work affordability, support/reservoir accounts, damping and drift.\",\n        \"Correlate inspected representative images with numerical observations; visual appeal cannot override failed local checks.\",\n        \"Deliver reproducible commands and a self-contained continue/reject/inconclusive recommendation with limits and remaining uncertainty.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-contents\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-boundary\",\n        \"C-resources\",\n        \"C-experiment\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes I12 active simulation, I13 visible fixture and D1/D9 frozen budgets. Capabilities: simulation-health (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md), traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; references/tracing-diagnostics.md), snapshots-checkpoints (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md; references/visual-qa.md). Reuse component checks and monitors; record horizon justification, inspections and stopping rationale. No population timing before favorable review.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I12\",\n        \"I13\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Qualify the full active single chamber before scaling the workload.\",\n      \"id\": \"I14\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-active\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the active single chamber preserve the approved local physical behavior and cumulative balances through refinement, resource cycles and extended horizons, or do transport, affordability or drift findings invalidate expansion to the population screen?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Qualify the active single chamber\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"I15 produces a reproducible shared-fluid screen at accepted quality and a specific adopt/reject/inconclusive foundation recommendation.\",\n        \"The conclusion states that the screen does not establish freely interacting biological-world readiness and stops this plan.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-resources\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Grouping record only. No future implementation or speculative performance infrastructure is included.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"goal\": \"Measure the bounded population pilot and conclude the foundation experiment.\",\n      \"id\": \"M-screen\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Screen shared-fluid cost and decide\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Before timing, retain an immutable workload/configuration specification: 16 active separated chambers, one shared 128 by 128 exterior grid, at most 128 membrane vertices each, fixed coefficients/activity/geometry, accepted quality limits and supports preventing contact.\",\n        \"Show meaningful continued activity and shared-fluid response using semantic observations; do not lower quality or activity to reach the cost target.\",\n        \"On Ryzen 9 9950X3D with at most 16 CPU workers, measure complete advancement including coupling iterations, failed attempts/retries and state/geometry updates; report simulated/wall time, latency distribution and extremes, memory and worker count.\",\n        \"Document measurement protocol, repetitions and variability; report rendering and diagnostics overhead separately without excluding costs essential to valid advancement.\",\n        \"Compare against one simulated second per wall-clock second at accepted quality; unavailable hardware or exhausted evidence budgets produce an inconclusive conclusion where appropriate.\",\n        \"Deliver exact reproduction commands, retained evidence and an adopt/reject/inconclusive recommendation with physical and performance limitations. Do not launch an unapproved optimization or solver-replacement campaign.\"\n      ],\n      \"components\": [\n        \"C-world\",\n        \"C-experiment\",\n        \"C-fluid\",\n        \"C-structure\",\n        \"C-resources\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": \"Consumes favorably reviewed I14 and D1/D9 workload/budgets; otherwise blocked. Use bitloop (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md; .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md), traces (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md; references/tracing-diagnostics.md) and simulation-health (.mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md; references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md). Freeze the final workload before evaluation, with no threshold changes absent a human decision. Use existing timing facilities or minimal scoped timers, not a benchmarking platform. AS-cost applies; conclusions belong in supported result fields with numerical observations, not artifact links alone.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"I14\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether the qualified primitive meets the bounded shared-fluid pilot cost target.\",\n      \"id\": \"I15\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"M-screen\",\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"At unchanged accepted quality and meaningful activity, does the frozen 16-chamber shared-grid evidence support adopting this foundation for a subsequent plan, or do complete-step cost, variability, hardware limitations or physical failures require rejection or an inconclusive decision?\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Screen shared-fluid cost and conclude\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"vision_summary\": \"Design, obtain approval for, implement and qualify one supported deformable chamber with actual contents inertia and pressure, two-way exterior-fluid coupling, finite-rate nutrient uptake and fuel-limited actuation. Prove the passive foundation before resources, qualify the active single chamber before a frozen 16-chamber shared-fluid cost screen, and end with a reproducible foundation decision rather than expanding into the eventual biological world.\"\n}",
